description:
List or change your own brain settings (only yours; your definition and other agents do not change). Changes work from your next brain call. model picks the brain; the other keys (like temperature, max_tokens) only tune its answers. One op per call:
- list: {"op": "ls"}  (one KEY=VALUE per line; add "long": true to see which keys you changed)
- change: {"op": "set", "settings": {"model": "smart-high", "temperature": "0.2"}}  (values are strings; a key your body does not read is kept, with a warning)
- undo some changes: {"op": "rm", "keys": ["temperature"]}
- undo all your changes: {"op": "reset"}
If you set a brain that does not work, you stop answering until a human fixes it; use ls first. Errors: ArgumentsBad, OpUnknown, KeyMissing, LlmMissing, LlmBad, DaemonMissing, DaemonFailed, InstanceMissing. Details: knowledge_read aos/me.json#/self_llm.
